view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Refs KS-2029: AgentMailMessage declares created_at and timestamp, which the poll's date line reads\n\n**TIER 2: test-only and type-only. One e2e fixture file gains two optional interface members and a two-line comment (+4), and a flow and a cheat fragment are added. No product byte, no runtime line, no export changes.** Merge to develop only. Whether the ticket is finished by this is the board seat's call, so this PR says `Refs`.\n\nLinear: https://linear.app/secuura/issue/KS-2029\n\n## Summary\n\n- **What changes.** In `Blockchain/Dev/tests/e2e/tests/fixtures/test-helpers.ts` the interface `AgentMailMessage` (lines 66 to 75 at develop `13e62febfba8`) declared `received_at` and no other date field, while the poll helper's date line (113 at develop, 117 after this change) reads `msg.received_at || msg.created_at || msg.timestamp`. TypeScript reported two TS2339 errors there, at (113,59) and (113,77), exactly as the ticket says. The interface now also declares `created_at?: string` and `timestamp?: string`, after `received_at`, with a two-line why-and-ticket comment above them. The date line itself is not touched.\n- **Why optional members (shape a) and not a deleted fallback (shape b).** Optional members make the existing fallback type-correct without claiming the mail API returns those fields. Deleting the two fallbacks would change what the helper does at run time against a mail API whose fields nobody measured.\n- **Not claimed.** No repository-defined leg type-checks `tests/e2e`: its `package.json` scripts are Playwright runners and a readiness check, and the root `check:test-types` covers five services only. So the proof below is a hand-run type check, not a gate. Which date fields the mail API really sends, and which Playwright version the e2e package's own install would select (it declares `^1.40`; the root install is 1.61.1, and the check used the root copy), are not measured. The workflow steps `ci:e2e` and `quality:static` run in `systemTest/playwright`, a different package: a search of `systemTest` finds no file importing this fixture (control: 14 files there import `@playwright/test`).\n- **Readers of the interface.** 20 files under `tests/e2e` contain the import path `fixtures/test-helpers`; exactly one other file names `AgentMailMessage`, `tests/email-notifications.prelaunch.spec.ts`. None is changed here, and none was type-checked by me: adding optional members only widens what the type allows, but that was not run.\n\n## Test plan / Test Evidence\n\n**Host and runtime (stated per the repo's test-discipline skill).** Every run below was made on one Apple Silicon Mac (arm64, Darwin 27.2.0), with no Docker stack started (the change is a type declaration; nothing here reaches a database or a mail server). Node is v26.8.1, the only Node on this machine; it is NOT the long-term-support line the repo's `CLAUDE.md` names (Node 24 today), nothing was run on Node 24, and the long-term-support status of Node 26 was not checked. Load1 at the starts was 2 to 4.\n\n**Touched:** three files: `Blockchain/Dev/tests/e2e/tests/fixtures/test-helpers.ts` (+4 -0) and the new flow and cheat fragments `KS-2029-agentmailmessage-declares-the-two-fields-the-poll-reads.html` (+17 and +4). Base is develop `13e62febfba8` (the squash of PR 2213). The census at the cut (GraphQL, all pages, 102 open pull requests, 455 file rows, positive and negative controls pass) finds no open PR on any of the three paths and none anywhere under `Blockchain/Dev/tests/e2e/`.\n\n**Ran** (by Seat R 113th, 2026-11-12, in tree `s-r113-ks2029`; evidence `evidence/row48/`):\n- **The hand-run type check** (TypeScript 5.9.3 from the hoisted root install, `--noEmit --target es2022 --module esnext --moduleResolution bundler --skipLibCheck --strict --types node`), on the file in the tree and on a scratch copy with the install linked beside it. The unchanged file at develop: exactly two errors, `(113,59)` and `(113,77)`, both TS2339, exit 2. The changed file: no error, exit 0. A planted third undeclared member read on the date line (`msg.zzz_planted`): exactly one new TS2339, at `(117,94)`, exit 2, so the check reads the file.\n- **docs-fragments check:** OK (flow 117 legacy + 237 new, cheat 112 legacy + 237 new). **`npm run audit:gate`:** OK (5 distinct advisories reported, 5 baselined). **`npm run check:test-types`:** exit 0 once `packages/shared/dist` was built in the tree (it covers five services, not `tests/e2e`).\n- **`eslint`** on the fixture (absolute path): exit 0 with the warning \"File ignored because no matching configuration was supplied\": no lint configuration covers `tests/e2e`, so lint did NOT run on it.\n\n**NOT run:** any e2e spec (they need a running stack and none was up); a type check of the spec files that import the fixture; Node 24; the four platform suites (Schemathesis, Akto, Playwright, k6); any run against the live demo or the local Docker stack; any CI run (retired for this repo). The pre-push hook's legs (below) run the repo's checks on the pushed head.\n\n**Docs fragments and changed-line comments (the repo's test-discipline skill).** A flow and a cheat fragment describe the change (the check passes with or without them; the skill's section 4 owes the pair for a test change), the flow one with the section-number token, and both added members carry a why-and-ticket comment.\n\n**Migrations + config:** none.\n\n**Pre-push hook:** (quoted from the push of this head)\n```\nPREFLIGHT INCOMPLETE — 13/16 legs ran, 3 SKIPPED. Nothing failed.\n  legs 3 4 8 — local stack not up; you can clear this by starting it.\n  This is NOT a pass. Do not quote it as one — say which legs ran.\n```\n- Leg 14, verbatim: `shell suites: 127 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped (of 127)`\n\n## Before this deploys\n\n- Nothing deploys from this PR: it changes a type declaration in an e2e fixture and two documentation fragments. It reaches develop only; \"deployed\" reads as \"on develop\".\n\n## Notes for the gate\n\n- **The behaviour that matters:** none at run time. The only effect is what TypeScript says about the interface; the poll helper's date line is unchanged.\n- **What the proof does not see.** It reads one file with the root install's TypeScript and Playwright types; it does not read the e2e package's own install, the spec files that use the helper, or the mail API.\n- Branch name `feature/ks-2029-testse2e-fixtures` is Linear's own suggestion for the ticket.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-12T11:12:29Z","updated_at":"2026-11-12T11:12:37Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"0f74b3fd38706d6a851c488eed937f0d3fdc0f65","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"Secuura:feature/ks-2029-testse2e-fixtures","ref":"feature/ks-2029-testse2e-fixtures","repo":{"id":1170327089,"node_id":"R_kgDORcHGMQ","name":"Distributed_Secuura","full_name":"Secuura/Distributed_Secuura","owner":{"login":"Secuura","id":257240886,"node_id":"O_kgDOD1UvNg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257240886?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Secuura","html_url":"https://github.com/Secuura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Secuura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Secuura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Secuura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Secuura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Secuura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Secuura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Secuura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Secuura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Secuura/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_ad